Package: castSDM
Type: Package
Title: Auditable Scenario Comparisons for Species Distribution Models
Version: 0.28.1
Authors@R: c(
    person(
            "Liqiang", "Q",
      email = "2759831686@qq.com",
      role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
      comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0002-6966-4633")
    )
  )
Description: Auditable model-conditional comparisons of environmental scenarios
    using species distribution models. A paired 2 x 2 design separates two
    predictor groups, their joint change and interaction with fixed model
    weights, finite-domain checks, training-support diagnostics and paired
    model disagreement. Tables and bounded-memory raster processing share one
    contrast kernel. Random forest, MaxEnt and generalized additive model
    engines support variable screening, spatial cross-validation and full-data
    refitting. Content-verified stage caches and execution receipts support
    reproducible workflows. Contrasts describe fitted suitability responses;
    they do not establish real-world causal effects or occurrence probabilities.
